raylib
------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  https://github.com/raysan5/raylib
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng licence.

  raylib is not copied into this repository. It is referenced as a git
  submodule (`jank-raylib-sys/raylib`) pinned to an upstream commit, fetched
  from raysan5/raylib on first build and compiled from source by
  `jank-raylib-sys/jank-build.bb`.

  One patch is applied to that checkout at build time:
  `jank-raylib-sys/patches/macos-opengl43-forward-compat.patch`. It adds the
  `#if defined(__APPLE__)` GLFW forward-compatibility guard that raylib's
  own RL_OPENGL_33 branch already has but its RL_OPENGL_43 branch is
  missing. This is an alteration to raylib's source, applied only in a local
  working tree and never redistributed; see that directory's README.md for
  the full rationale.


raylib examples
---------------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5) and contributors
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng licence.

  The example programs under `raylib-examples/src/raylib_examples/` are
  ports of raylib's own example programs to jank. They are altered versions:
  the logic is reimplemented in jank, and the interop constraints described
  in docs/guide/ forced structural changes throughout. Every example's
  docstring names the upstream C source it was ported from (e.g.
  `core/core_basic_window`, `shapes/shapes_bouncing_ball`), and
  `raylib-examples/README.md` lists the same mapping in table form.

  One deliberate behavioural deviation from the originals, applied
  uniformly: every example sets FLAG_WINDOW_HIGHDPI.


rlights.h
---------
  Copyright (c) 2017-2024 Victor Fisac (@victorfisac) and
                          Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng licence.

  `jank-raylib-sys/include/jank_rlights.h` is an altered version of
  raylib's `examples/shaders/rlights.h`. CreateLight and UpdateLightValues
  are kept verbatim from the original and marked `static`; the surrounding
  index-based scalar wrappers and per-type uniform setters are new work,
  needed because jank functions can neither take nor return native values.
  The file's own header comment carries the same attribution.


jank-raylib-sys and jank-build-cmake
------------------------------------
  Copyright (c) Kyle Cesare (@kylc)
  https://github.com/kylc/lein-jank-playground
  Licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0.

  The `jank-raylib-sys` wrapper and the overall lein-jank project layout
  originate from Kyle Cesare's lein-jank-playground. This repository carries
  them forward with modifications: lein-jank bumped to 2026.06-1, an
  `include` verbatim-path added to ship the jank-helper headers, a second
  include-dir build directive emitted for them, an explicit OPENGL_VERSION
  pin, and lib/lib64 detection for cross-distro shared-library layout.

  The `cmake-build` function in `jank-raylib-sys/jank-build.bb` is inlined
  from that project's `org.clojars.kylc/jank-build-cmake` 0.1-SNAPSHOT
  (`jank/build/cmake.bb`), behaviour unchanged. It is vendored rather than
  depended on so a fresh clone builds without fetching a floating SNAPSHOT
  from a third party's Clojars account.


